      "writtenOn": "2018-05-25T03:53:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Port 80’s written data can be latched into BRAM and it is a hardware mechanism. But there will be no interrupt when the queue has data. \nWe have to enable a logic device (PM3) and set the base address at 80h, so we are able to get an interrupt when host output data to port 80.\n\nP80LC is read-only.",
      "parentUuid": "1aeae4ae_8cc6bb3d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 40
